# @hsk-sync:visual-markdown

Token `@hsk-sync:visual-markdown` marks one **Visual Markdown** WYSIWYG editor in two apps. If toolbar commands, Markdown round-trip, YAML handling, or image insert behavior change in either implementation, update the other to match.

## Sibling implementations

| Block | Path |
|-------|------|
| VS Code host | `D:\GitHub\harrix-swiss-knife\vscode\harrix-notes-explorer-hsk\visual-editor.js` |
| VS Code webview | `D:\GitHub\harrix-swiss-knife\vscode\harrix-notes-explorer-hsk\media\visual-editor.js` + `media\visual-editor.css` |
| Android (this repo) | `app/src/main/assets/visual-editor/` + `NotesVisualEditorPane.kt` |

## Shared contract

Toolbar (same commands, same order):

1. Bold, italic, strikethrough, inline code
2. H1, H2, H3, paragraph
3. Bullet list, numbered list, blockquote
4. Link, image, horizontal rule

Markdown I/O:

- Parse body with **marked** (GFM, `breaks: false`)
- Serialize with **Turndown** (`atx` headings, fenced code, `*` emphasis, `-` lists, `---` hr)
- YAML front matter stays in a separate box (`---` … `---`), not in the contenteditable body
- Local images keep a Markdown-relative `data-md-src` (typically `img/…`)

Images:

- Image button / paste / drop copies files into the note's `img/` folder
- Inserted HTML uses `data-md-src` so Turndown writes `![](img/name.ext)`

Out of scope for this sync id: VS Code theme tokens, Android Material theme, SAF vs filesystem, host dialogs (link prompt / file picker chrome).

When adding a **new format command or insert kind**, add it to both toolbars and both JS round-trips in the same change set.
